name>Bockaert</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>NMDA-dependent superoxide production and neurotoxicity</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1993</year><volume>364</volume><fpage>535</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7687749</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/364535a0</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mutel</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Buchy</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Klingelschmidt</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Messer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bleuel</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Kemp</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Richards</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>In vitro binding properties in rat brain of [3H]Ro 25-6981, a potent and selective antagonist of NMDA receptors containing NR2B subunits</article-title><source>J Neurochem</source><year>1998</year><volume>70</volume><fpage>2147</fpage><lpage>55</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9572302</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>WT</given-names></name><name><surname>Kuo</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Mishra</surname><given-names>OP</given-names></name><name><surname>Delivoria-Papadopoulos</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Distribution and expression of the subunits of N-methyl-D-aspartate (NMDA) receptors; NR1, NR2A and NR2B in hypoxic newborn piglet brains</article-title><source>Brain Res</source><year>1998</year><volume>799</volume><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>54</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9666074</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0006-8993(98)0